{
  "summary": "Fixes `test_orphanage_dos_many` in `p2p_opportunistic_1p1c.py` so that it actually saturates the orphan pool limit and triggers eviction. Instead of having 60 peers send duplicate orphan transactions as `tx` messages (which are ignored without registering new announcers), only the first peer sends `tx` messages while the remaining 59 peers send `inv` announcements, and the test asserts that 3000 announcements are recorded.",
  "problem": "In `test_orphanage_dos_many`, duplicate orphan transactions sent via `tx` messages are dropped in `ReceivedTx` without recording sender peer IDs. Because of this, the orphanage peaked at only 152 announcements rather than the 3000-announcement limit, so eviction was never tested and a node with broken eviction logic would still pass the test.",
  "evidence": [
    "The author observed that the test passed vacuously: 'The orphanage peaks at 152 announcements against a limit of 3000, so nothing is evicted.'",
    "The author verified that 'If LimitOrphans is changed to evict the normal peer's orphan first, the test used to pass and now fails.'"
  ],
